  "label": "User projected onto the smiling Muslim man in the top panel",
  "description": "The user is projected onto the visual material of the smiling man labeled 'muslim' in the top panel. The user is expected to see themselves in this figure, interpreting the man's indifference as a representation of how Muslims are supposedly reacting to the Christchurch shootings. This projection is implicit, as the meme does not use explicit deictic pronouns like 'you' or 'me', but the viewer is invited to identify with the figure as a representative of the Muslim community being stereotyped.",
